s-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/low-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/low-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/low-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Low severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> Test optional registry metric allowance</summary>\n\n`tools/\u200brunner/\u200btests/\u200btest_checks.py:294`\n\nThis test passes even if `allowed=set(spec.allowed_metrics)` is removed, because `_seen_expected_names()` already filters out optional non-registry metrics. As a non-blocking test improvement, include an optional registry metric and parameterize its count as zero and one so the test detects regressions in the allowance behavior.\n</details>\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>1 resolved since last review</strong></summary>\n\n- <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Medium severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> [Restrict Cassandra driver dependency updates to versions below 4.4](https://github.com/open-telemetry/semantic-conventions-conformance/pull/135#discussion_r4373220784)\n</details>\n\n<sub>Review effort: Balanced</sub>","comment_id":null,"key":"review:5646471971","kind":"body","line":null,"path":null,"review_id":5646471971}],"frozen_at":1792979086,"frozen_at_iso":"2026-10-26T01:44:46Z","frozen_sha":"a0a82a77ee792e3cd46336c9a1ec34dcaa5a052b","head_ref":"trask-add-cassandra-conformance","head_repo":"open-telemetry/semantic-conventions-conformance","head_repo_id":1324141285,"input_mode":"direct","launch_run":{"actor_id":218610,"attempt":1,"id":40251830392},"loop_kind":"copilot_review","metadata":{"body":"Adds Java Cassandra conformance for the stable database semantic conventions. The database runner now starts a pinned Cassandra 5.0.9 container and runs simple queries, prepared statements, logged batches, and server-reported query errors against driver 3.11.5, driver 4.3.1, and Apache driver 4.19.3.\n\nThe Java agent covers all three driver lines. The published `opentelemetry-cassandra-4.4` library instrumentation runs against Apache driver 4.19.3. Earlier driver lines remain agent-only because OpenTelemetry does not publish standalone instrumentation for them.\n\nScenario contracts can now declare `allowed_metrics` alongside required `metrics`. Cassandra uses this to require `db.client.operation.duration` while accepting optional Java SDK and exporter self-metrics.\n","title":"Add Java Cassandra database conformance"},"mode":"publish","pr":135,"protocol":"git-candidate-v1","publication":{"auth_mode":"fine_grained_pat","authorized_actor_id":218610,"authorized_at":1792976257,"generation":8,"max_pipelines":5,"phase":"5074dfd6c1c64f239a346a29f4fc8dd1","profile":"git-candidate-v1","required_checks":[]},"repo":"open-telemetry/semantic-conventions-conformance","repo_id":1324141285,"request_id":"1ae99c5ad3444226a83272c181965416","schema":2,"source_private":false,"target_private":false,"workflow_ref":"review-loop-revisions/f9d2af9fce01ee319295abe00856608a264119f4","workflow_revision":"f9d2af9fce01ee319295abe00856608a264119f4"},"run":{"attempt":1,"conclusion":"success","id":40255844471,"url":"https://github.com/trask/copilot-workflows/actions/runs/40255844471"},"schema":2,"seen_findings":["03ada8f0b3850e9b5f3245aa345ce024a46a307f92dc8f027dfb8661b4aa4ae0","91078c31fa08df1a4f7216321aa217b85d06e9181fc39427fc2f9b2d57aeb30d"],"seen_inline_findings":["fb84ef39189015d5a6b4d944